@startuml context-map
' Origin: drafted with AI assistance (Claude Code) from docs/03-bounded-contexts.md; reviewed by the author.
title StudyAnchor — context map (DDD strategic design)
skinparam rectangle {
  RoundCorner 15
}
left to right direction

rectangle "Planner context\n(core: what / when / why)\nCourse, Topic, Deadline, Availability,\nStudyPlan, TimeBlock, Goal,\nValueStatement, Reminder" as P
rectangle "Tutor context\n(core: active learning)\nMaterial, TutoringSession,\nMessage, TopicReference (read model)" as T
rectangle "Focus context\n(core: sustained focus)\nFocusSession, Distraction,\nFocusProgress" as F
rectangle "Social context\n(supporting: accountability)\nFriendship, StudyRoom,\nSharingSetting, Presence" as S

P --> T : "U → D (Tutor = conformist)\nTopicCreated, TopicDeleted"
T --> P : "U → D\nMaterialAdded,\nUnderstandingRecorded"
F --> P : "U → D\nFocusSessionStarted/Ended,\nDistractionSpikeDetected"
F --> S : "U → D\nFocusSessionStarted/Ended\n(presence KTable)"
P ..> F : "REST (customer–supplier)\nGET /progress/{userId}"

note bottom of F
  Published language: JSON events in docs/05-events.md.
  Each service has its own Java records (no shared library).
end note
@enduml
